{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Rachel said, 'Elohim has judged me.'</b> When Bilhah, Rachel's maidservant, bore the first son, Rachel said, 'Elohim has judged me (דנני).' And a person ought to be careful with all his words, even with the opening of his words. Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, already expounded: four opened with 'אף' and perished from the world. And they are: the serpent, the chief butler, the congregation of Korah, and Haman. And you already know the end of Rachel, that she died in giving birth, for the attribute of judgment was stretched out against her." "<b>And you should understand</b> how she called his name Dan, for she explained in his name what Leah alluded to in the name Reuben. And since the attribute of judgment is included in mercy, therefore she added further to say, 'and also He has heard my voice,' corresponding to Simeon. And the second she called Naphtali, corresponding to HaShem the righteous; and this too is from below upward."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:28.319429584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}